# Zero Trust Device Authentication using RF Fingerprints

A machine learning-based device authentication project that uses Radio Frequency (RF) fingerprints to identify and authenticate wireless devices within a Zero Trust security framework.

## Overview

Traditional authentication methods often rely on credentials, device identifiers, or network-level trust. This project explores a Zero Trust approach where devices are continuously evaluated based on their unique RF characteristics.

The system uses RF fingerprinting and machine learning to distinguish between devices based on characteristics present in their wireless signals.

The main objective is to improve device authentication by treating every device as untrusted until its identity is verified.

## Key Features

- RF fingerprint-based device identification
- Machine learning-based authentication
- Zero Trust security approach
- Wireless device classification
- Feature extraction from RF signal data
- Model training and evaluation
- Authentication decision based on predicted device identity

