## Advantages

- Device authentication based on physical RF characteristics
- Reduces reliance on static device identifiers
- Can complement traditional authentication mechanisms
- Fits the Zero Trust security model
- Can be integrated with machine learning-based security systems

## Limitations

- RF characteristics can be affected by environmental conditions.
- Performance depends on the quality and diversity of RF data.
- Models trained on a limited set of devices may not generalize to unseen devices.
- Real-world deployment requires testing under different channel and hardware conditions.
- RF fingerprinting should be considered an additional authentication mechanism rather than the sole security control.

